# SmartCura MQTT access control list.
#
# Two kinds of client connect to this broker:
#
# 1. The worker's ingestion bridge — one service account that subscribes to
#    every device's vitals topic. Its username is "smartcura-bridge".
#
# 2. IoT devices — each connects with its UUIDv7 device_id as the username and
#    may publish only to its own vitals topic. The pattern rule below uses %u
#    (the authenticated username) so every device is covered by a single line
#    without per-device entries.
#
# The backend re-validates that the username matches the topic segment in
# mqtt-ingestion.handler.ts, so even a broker misconfiguration cannot turn into
# a cross-patient write without the handler also failing.

# Bridge: subscribe to all device vitals topics.
user smartcura-bridge
topic read smartcura/v1/devices/+/vitals

# Devices: each may publish only to its own vitals topic.
# %u is replaced with the authenticated username (the device's UUIDv7 id).
pattern write smartcura/v1/devices/%u/vitals
